<h1 id="neatlog-title" style="color:#0d47a1;font-size:1.5em;font-weight:700;border-bottom:2px solid #90caf9;padding-bottom:0.25em;margin-top:0"><code>neatlog</code> — operator logging standard</h1>

**`utils/neat_logger*`** is the repo’s **preferred unified** operator log producer (tagging, colors, file mirror, **Heartbeat**). Use it for **any** script, CLI, `python -m …` entrypoint, batch runner, or live harness — not only “long” jobs.

**Pair with:** **`.cursor/rules/opslog-ops-run-logs-directory.mdc`**, **`.cursor/rules/serlog-search-gitignored-logs.mdc`**.

<h2 id="neatlog-outline" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">Document outline</h2>

