<h2 id="neatlog-default" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. Default — always neat_logger for operators</h2>

| Context | Rule |
|---------|------|
| **CLI / `__main__` / ops script** | **Use neat_logger** (Python **`utils/neat_logger`**, TS **`utils/neat_logger_ts`**) — see **`HOWTO_USE_NEAT_LOGGER.md`**. |
| **Library pure functions** (no process story) | No forced logger; callers log at boundaries. |
| **Refactor plan** adds or changes a runner/harness | Plan **Quality bar** names log file + checkpoint ([§5](#neatlog-plan)). |
| **`qimpl` / `aciub` / `implref`** | Same phase ships logging — not deferred polish. |

**Patterns:**

- **`NeatLoggerFactory.create("OPS", "<COMPONENT>", log_file_name=…, log_output="both")`** for dedicated runs under **`logs/ops/`**.
- **`step` / `info` / `warning` / `error`** at transitions; **`heartbeat(...)`** around any call that may stay silent **&gt; ~20 s** (LLM, large HTTP read).
- Never **`print()`** alone for operator-visible progress in new harness code.

