<h2 id="neatlog-tailored" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. logging_utils — structured checkpoint only</h2>

**`logging_utils/`** complements neat_logger — it does **not** replace it.

| Use logging_utils for | Keep on neat_logger |
|-----------------------|---------------------|
| Append-only **JSONL** (`progress` / `result` events) | Human **`tail -f`** story |
| **`--resume`** key sets | Tags, colors, heartbeats |
| Dedup-friendly machine records | Errors with stack context |

Example: **`logging_utils/run_progress.py`** + **`NeatLoggerFactory`** in the retail lane runner.

