<h2 id="neatlog-debug" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Density: INFO + DEBUG</h2>

**Prefer more logging over less** when building or debugging runners (including multi-lane eval).

| Level | When |
|-------|------|
| **INFO / step** | Every milestone an operator should see in a normal run (start/end, lane, question_id, step name, i/N). |
| **DEBUG** | Branch choices, model ids, truncated prompt/hash sizes, top-k paths, HTTP status, retry attempt — anything that answers “what did it think right before it failed?” |

**Python:** `NeatLogger.debug(msg)` — emits only when **`NEAT_LOGGER_DEBUG=1`** (or `true` / `yes`). Plans and harness READMEs should document the env var for live debugging.

**Plans:** For eval/harness phases, Quality bar should say: *“DEBUG lines for retrieval/LLM boundaries; operator enables with NEAT_LOGGER_DEBUG.”*

