<h2 id="neatlog-checkpoint" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Checkpoint semantics — deducing the failing ticket</h2>

When **`results.jsonl`** is appended **sequentially**:

| Last line type | Inference |
|----------------|-----------|
| **`type: result`** | Last **completed** `(lane, question_id)` — success through judge/score. |
| **`type: progress`** with **`step: judge_start`** (no later **`row_done`** / **`result`**) | **Failing ticket** = that lane + question_id; failure likely **during judge** (or timeout waiting on judge). |
| **`step: answer_done`** then crash | Problem ticket = same ids; failure on **judge** (or between answer and judge). |
| **`step: row_error`** | Explicit failing ticket + error string. |

**Required for long benchmarks:** flush JSONL **before and after** slow external calls; never only write **`results.json`** at end.

